    {
      "tag": "succession_instability",
      "layer": "dynastic_legitimacy",
      "description": "The Nasrid civil war between Abu al-Hasan Ali, his son Boabdil, and his brother Muhammad al-Zaghal allowed Ferdinand and Isabella to support the weaker claimant (Boabdil) and exploit the division; Boabdil's eventual capitulation ended the emirate",
