    {
      "tag": "external_military_pressure",
      "layer": "military_security",
      "description": "Ferdinand and Isabella's systematic 10-year military campaign (1482–1492) used superior siege artillery to reduce Granada's mountain fortresses one by one; the loss of Málaga (1487) cut the kingdom off from Moroccan reinforcement by sea",
      "sources": [
        {
          "type": "wikidata",
